@startuml frontend_product_boundary
' Backend source baseline: origin/main 63adc08cf5c57e3a7cc3caa317452062606ce8b4.
' Frontend interaction-refinement baseline: origin/main 1813c601101660a401e5e2004c5c00b8e3d7b75b.
' Source evidence: frontend/src/App.vue (createSession, resumeSession, submit, product shell).
' Source evidence: frontend/src/composables/useRuntimeApi.ts (useRuntimeApi, requestRaw, consumeSse).
' Source evidence: frontend/src/projectors/runtimeEventProjector.ts (projectRuntimeEvents).
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/web/RuntimeSessionController.java.
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/web/RuntimeEventController.java.
' Observed behavior: the product shell hides credentials and protocol fields, while its HTTP 1.38 transitional adapter still calls Runtime V1 directly.
' Target-only design: the production UI uses a public bridge; the mate-service Agent, Chat, Attachment, and public event contracts do not exist yet.
' Design reason: internal session identifiers, credentials, ETags, and raw SSE payloads must not cross the production browser boundary.

title CampusClaw product frontend boundary
left to right direction

actor "Campus user" as User
rectangle "Product frontend" as Frontend {
  component "Agent and chat workspace" as Workspace
  component "Product event projector" as Projector
  component "Direct runtime adapter\n(transition only)" as DirectAdapter
  component "Developer diagnostics\n(internal build only)" as Diagnostics
}

rectangle "mate-service" as Mate {
  component "Public chat API" as PublicApi
  component "Chat to session mapping" as Mapping
  component "Auth, policy, and event projection" as Policy
}

rectangle "CampusClaw Runtime V1" as Runtime {
  component "Session controllers" as Sessions
  component "Request-scoped SSE" as Stream
}

User --> Workspace : chat tasks
Workspace --> PublicApi : public HTTP and SSE
PublicApi --> Policy
Policy --> Mapping
Mapping --> Sessions : internal HTTP
Stream --> Policy : internal SSE events
Policy --> Projector : public safe events
Workspace ..> DirectAdapter : current integration
DirectAdapter ..> Sessions : internal HTTP and SSE
Diagnostics ..> Sessions : local diagnostics only

note bottom of Frontend
Product constraints:
- No Service URL or credential editor
- No raw Runtime sessionId, ETag, JSON, or SSE frames
- Agent, chat, and attachment metadata use public resources
- Transitional direct adapter is not a production boundary
end note

note bottom of Mate
Security hardening:
- Terminate browser authentication
- Authorize each action
- Project internal errors and events
- Do not byte-forward internal SSE
end note

note bottom of Runtime
Observed internal contract:
- 11 Session Runtime operations
- One active execution per Session
- Persistent Entry history plus transient progress events
end note
@enduml

@startuml assistant_rich_text_rendering
' Analyzed source baseline: origin/main 1813c601101660a401e5e2004c5c00b8e3d7b75b.
' Baseline evidence: frontend/src/components/ConversationTimeline.vue lines 37-49 used plain text interpolation.
' Baseline evidence: frontend/src/projectors/runtimeEventProjector.ts projectAssistantEvent preserved delta and completed text.
' Implemented source: frontend/src/markdown/richText.ts (parseAssistantMarkdown, safeExternalLink, splitStableMarkdown).
' Implemented source: frontend/src/components/AssistantRichText.ts (AssistantRichText, renderNode, renderCodeBlock).
' Implemented source: frontend/src/projectors/conversationRounds.ts (groupConversationTurns) and frontend/src/components/AgentRound.vue.
' Implemented source: frontend/src/components/ConversationTimeline.vue and frontend/src/style.css assistant-rich-text and round-action rules.
' Observed behavior: Runtime transports text rather than HTML, and completed events plus history are authoritative.
' Architecture change: the Assistant turn now keeps rawMarkdown and all preview, completion, and history paths use one renderer.
' Security hardening: raw HTML, remote Markdown images, relative routes, credential-bearing URLs, and dangerous schemes never become active DOM.
' Architecture change: copy actions are owned by an Agent round rather than an Assistant Entry or code block.
' Design reason: a controlled token-to-Vue projection makes model tables, lists, and code readable without trusting generated HTML, while one round action avoids repeated controls.

title Assistant safe rich-text rendering
top to bottom direction

rectangle "Runtime and public event input" as Input {
  component "assistant.message.delta\ntext fragment" as Delta
  component "assistant.message.completed\nfull persistent text" as Completed
  component "GET history\nfull persistent text" as History
}

rectangle "Conversation projection" as Projection {
  component "Assistant turn\nrawMarkdown and state" as Raw
  component "Stable block boundary\nplus plain streaming tail" as Stable
}

rectangle "Safe rich-text renderer" as Renderer {
  component "markdown-it token parser\nraw HTML disabled" as Parser
  component "Node allowlist\nURL policy and render budget" as Policy
  component "Fixed Vue VNodes\nno v-html or innerHTML" as Vue
}

rectangle "Assistant message UI" as UI {
  component "Paragraphs, headings,\nlists, tasks, and quotes" as Prose
  component "Scrollable semantic table" as Table
  component "Inline code and code block" as Code
  component "Safe external link" as Link
  component "Escaped plain-text fallback" as Fallback
  component "One Agent-round copy action" as RoundCopy
}

Delta --> Raw : append source text
Completed --> Raw : replace preview with authority
History --> Raw : restore the same source text
Raw --> Stable : once per animation frame
Stable --> Parser : stable blocks and safe tail
Parser --> Policy : parsed tokens
Policy --> Vue : allowed nodes and attributes
Policy --> Fallback : rejected or over budget
Vue --> Prose
Vue --> Table
Vue --> Code
Vue --> Link
Raw --> RoundCopy : aggregate Assistant source by User turn

note bottom of Input
Observed source contract:
- Runtime carries text, not HTML
- Completed and history are authoritative
- Tool result and safe thinking disclosure use separate UI paths
end note

note bottom of Renderer
Security rules:
- Escape raw HTML
- Allow only absolute HTTP and HTTPS links
- Block Markdown image network requests
- Clamp headings inside the message
- Preserve source text for fallback and round copy
end note

note bottom of UI
Responsive and accessibility rules:
- Only table and code containers scroll horizontally
- The page and composer never gain horizontal overflow
- Screen readers receive one completion announcement
- A completed Agent round exposes one copy icon
end note
@enduml

@startuml runtime_event_ui_projection
' Backend source baseline: origin/main 63adc08cf5c57e3a7cc3caa317452062606ce8b4.
' Frontend interaction-refinement baseline: origin/main 1813c601101660a401e5e2004c5c00b8e3d7b75b.
' Visual design baseline: campusclaw-frontend-design 5c2231654ea94dd248b5ea9a478d2cb27cd36a52.
' Source evidence: frontend/src/projectors/runtimeEventProjector.ts (projectRuntimeEvents, projectAssistantEvent, projectThinkingEvent, projectToolEvent, projectToolArguments).
' Source evidence: frontend/src/composables/useRuntimeApi.ts (dispatchSseFrame, mergeRuntimeEvent, loadHistory).
' Source evidence: frontend/src/projectors/conversationRounds.ts (groupConversationTurns, groupAgentBlocks).
' Source evidence: frontend/src/components/ConversationTimeline.vue, AgentRound.vue, ThinkingDisclosure.vue, ToolActivity.vue, and BrandMark.vue.
' Source evidence: frontend/src/assets/campusclaw-mark-o1.png and frontend/src/style.css.
' Source evidence: frontend/src/components/ComposerBox.vue (onKeydown, current follow-up mode).
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEventType.java (RuntimeEventType).
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEventProjector.java (projectMessageStart, projectMessageUpdate, projectToolStart, projectToolEnd).
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEntryCodec.java (toHistoryEvent, toSseData).
' Product-reference evidence: ChatGPT.app webview/assets/app-initial-BCLYDefw.js (followUpQueueMode, K9s) and webview/assets/zh-CN-ByRVSIXt.js.
' Observed behavior: HTTP 1.38 lowerCamelCase persistent entries and transient execution events share one request-scoped SSE response; Runtime thinking contains raw reasoning and no safe display summary.
' Observed Codex behavior: desktop follow-up mode defaults to steer; a modifier submits one message with the inverse mode.
' Security hardening: raw thinking is ignored; tool arguments are bounded and redacted before DOM projection.
' Architecture change: User turns bound Agent rounds; each completed round owns one copy action.
' Product constraint: each thinking item and each tool item owns an independent warm neutral dashed activity frame.
' Design reason: independent frames preserve compact safe activity while preventing one expanded tool from visually swallowing adjacent thinking or tool items.

title Runtime events to product UI projection
left to right direction

rectangle "Runtime event families" as Events {
  component "user.message" as UserEvent
  component "assistant.message.started\nassistant.message.delta\nassistant.message.completed" as AssistantEvents
  component "assistant.thinking.delta\nassistant.thinking.completed" as ThinkingEvents
  component "tool.execution.started\ntool.execution.completed\ntool.result" as ToolEvents
  component "session.status.idle\nstream.end\nstream.error" as TerminalEvents
}

rectangle "Frontend projection" as Projection {
  component "User turn" as UserTurn
  component "Streaming assistant turn" as AssistantTurn
  component "Safe thinking disclosure" as ThinkingDisclosure
  component "Compact tool disclosure\ninput then output" as ToolDisclosure
  component "Independent dashed\nthinking frame" as ThinkingFrame
  component "Independent dashed\ntool frame" as ToolFrame
  component "Agent round\none copy action" as AgentRound
  component "Exact O1 brand asset\nonce per Agent round" as BrandAsset
  component "Session and composer state" as SessionState
}

rectangle "User controls while running" as Controls {
  component "Adjust direction\n(default)" as Adjust
  component "Queue follow-up\n(configured or one-shot inverse)" as Continue
  component "Stop" as Stop
}

UserEvent --> UserTurn : persist and render
AssistantEvents --> AssistantTurn : preview then replace with final
ThinkingEvents --> ThinkingDisclosure : safe display fields or state only
ToolEvents --> ToolDisclosure : merge lifecycle and result
TerminalEvents --> SessionState : idle, complete, or recoverable error
ThinkingDisclosure --> ThinkingFrame
ToolDisclosure --> ToolFrame
AssistantTurn --> AgentRound
ThinkingFrame --> AgentRound
ToolFrame --> AgentRound
BrandAsset --> AgentRound

Adjust --> SessionState : internal steer
Continue --> SessionState : internal follow-up
Stop --> SessionState : internal abort

note bottom of ThinkingDisclosure
Never display raw delta or content.
The public bridge must provide a safe title
and summary. No thinking event means no frame.
An event without a display summary shows a
precise placeholder instead of raw reasoning.
The disclosure always remains expandable.
end note

note bottom of ToolDisclosure
Current and failed tools remain expanded.
Successful tool details collapse by default.
Arguments are row, depth, and length bounded.
Credentials and internal IDs are redacted.
Absolute paths are reduced to the last segment.
end note

note bottom of AgentRound
Use a User turn as the product round boundary.
Join non-empty Assistant rawMarkdown in order.
Exclude thinking and tool diagnostics from copy.
Hide the copy icon while the round is active.
end note

note bottom of SessionState
Network loss does not replay the POST.
Keep the submitted draft until user.message
or persistent history confirms a new Entry.
If confirmation is still missing, mark the
outcome uncertain and forbid blind retry.

Adjust direction does not interrupt the
current model call or tool execution.
end note
@enduml
